  "qualifications": [
    "Three sequential cohorts, two repetitions per mode and network; shared host and short windows.",
    "Each compressed file retains the complete original JSON bytes, including all samples and missed pings.",
    "Audio bytes include GLA1 headers, excluding WebSocket/TCP/IP overhead. Proxy bytes cover the entire session, including warmup.",
    "Browser CPU covers the stable CDP process endpoint intersection; it is not decoder-only cost. Native/guest CPU windows are measured separately.",
    "Decoder trace uses exact timestamps and excludes unmatched outputs; it is not a complete decoder latency distribution.",
    "Sampled playback and pending-output maxima can miss peaks between 50 ms observations.",
    "There is no source-to-speaker, moving-desktop, guest-input-response, real-WAN or music-quality measurement.",
    "Source commits identify native and embedded browser code; the same separately pinned benchmark sources were used for all three builds. Binary hashes identify measured files, not reproducible-build guarantees.",
    "The released baseline exposes no pendingDecodes counter; its recorded zero is a harness fallback, not an observation of hidden decoder work."
  ],
